      "status": "ok",
      "takeaway": "At the 2026-09-09 close of 104.18, on a 4.83% risk-free rate and a 8.88% WACC, the DCF values DIS at 79.29 a share on Gordon growth and 72.80 on the value driver, 76% and 70% of the price. No exit-multiple value is drawn; the note under the football field says why. Run backwards, the close earns 7.6% a year if the base case holds, or needs 13% revenue growth next year, a path 1016 of 1,662 TMT company-years ever compounded. Correlating the simulation's four drivers widens the spread of value by 22%.",
